    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Tests that {@link Days#parse(CharSequence)} accepts an ISO-8601 period text that carries a leading minus sign (e.g. {@code \"-P2D\"}). <p> Per the {@code parse} contract, a leading {@code \"-\"} negates the whole amount. Each case therefore takes a well-formed period text {@code str} whose day-value is {@code expectedDays}, prefixes it with {@code \"-\"}, and asserts that parsing yields the negated amount {@code Days.of(-expectedDays)}."
